FAQ = [
 ("What is the best tonneau cover for a Jeep Gladiator?",
  "For most owners, the BAKFlip MX4 448701. It has polymer-reinforced aluminum panels, a 400 lb evenly distributed rating, auto-latches and a 5-year warranty. BAK says it installs in 30 minutes or less and works with or without the Trail Rail system. RealTruck lists it at $1,099.99. If you want a hard cover for half that, the Gator EFX GC34010 is $549 and is a favorite on JeepGladiatorForum. For full-bed access with a hard surface, look at the TruXedo Sentry or BAK Revolver X2 roll-ups."),
 ("Do tonneau covers work with the Gladiator Trail Rail system?",
  "Most name-brand covers do, but check the listing. RealTruck's fitment for the BAKFlip MX4, Gator EFX, TruXedo Sentry and BAK Revolver X2 says each is compatible with or without Trail Rail, and Tyger says the T3 fits \"with or without Utility Track System\". Some cheaper listings are sold in separate with-rail and without-rail versions. Gator's own ETX soft tri-fold, for example, is listed \"w/o track rail\". If your bed has rails on the sides and front, find those words in the title."),
 ("What is the Gladiator Trail Rail system?",
  "It is Jeep's cargo management system: a 52 in front rail and two 48 in side rails bolted to the bed, with sliding cleats and optional utility cross rails. Jeep sells the same rails as a Mopar accessory (82215956), described as identical to the production system, for $492.20 on Jeep's gear store. Each rail side is rated for 250 lb vertical load. The rails sit along the bed walls where some cover clamps mount, which is why fitment calls them out."),
 ("How long is the Jeep Gladiator bed?",
  "Every 2020–2026 Gladiator has the same 5 ft bed. Tonneau makers list it as 60 in or 60.3 in. The only cab is the four-door crew cab, and Sport, Willys, Mojave, Rubicon and the rest of the trims share the same box. You don't need to measure to choose a length. What you do need to check is Trail Rail compatibility and, if you have a soft top, how the cover's security depends on the tailgate."),
 ("Is a hard tonneau cover secure on a Gladiator?",
  "Only as secure as the tailgate. Every folding and roll-up cover here locks because its rear edge sits under a closed, locked tailgate. On the Gladiator, the tailgate lock is tied to the power locks, and owners on JeepGladiatorForum point out that a thief who cuts through a soft top can reach the unlock button. Some owners unplug the tailgate's electric lock actuator so only the key opens it. BAK lists the MX4 as not recommended for soft-top trucks."),
 ("Does a tonneau cover affect the Gladiator's tailgate?",
  "No. The covers here seal against the top edge of the tailgate but don't attach to it, so the tailgate still drops normally. It can also stay in the partially open position its hinges and support cables allow for longer loads. With the cover closed and the tailgate lowered, the rear edge of the cover is unlocked and can be lifted, so close the tailgate before you leave the truck parked."),
 ("Hard or soft cover — which is better on a Gladiator?",
  "Buy a hard cover if gear stays in the bed overnight or you run a hardtop. The MX4, Gator EFX, Sentry and Revolver X2 carry 300 to 400 lb spread evenly and resist a knife. A soft cover such as the $221 Tyger T3 weighs 28.4 lb, installs in minutes and comes off quickly, which suits owners who swap between a bed rack and a cover or haul camping gear taller than the bed walls."),
 ("Can I use a bed rack with a tonneau cover on a Gladiator?",
  "Sometimes. Because the Gladiator's roof comes off, bed racks are the usual way to carry a rooftop tent or gear. A folding cover generally has to be removed or folded before a rack goes on, unless the rack is made to sit over the cover. Mopar's Trail Rail cross rails and racks built for over-cover use are the usual combinations. If a rack is planned, pick it first, then choose a cover the rack maker lists as compatible."),
 ("Do I need to drill to install a Gladiator tonneau cover?",
  "No. Every cover here clamps inside the bed rails. BAK and Gator quote 30 minutes or less for the MX4 and EFX, TruXedo and BAK quote under an hour for the Sentry and Revolver X2, and Tyger says 5–10 minutes for the T3. The usual complication is an over-rail bedliner, which Tyger says needs small holes cut for its clamps. Under-rail and spray-in liners need nothing."),
 ("Is the factory Mopar tonneau cover worth it?",
  "Jeep's optional folding tonneau has a \"Weekend Warrior\" mode that lets you close the tailgate while hauling 2x4 lumber in the bed. Owners on JeepGladiatorForum note it can't be opened without first opening the tailgate. It is a sound choice if you order it with the truck. Buying aftermarket, the MX4 and EFX give you published load ratings (400 lb and 300 lb) and warranties you can compare directly."),
]

